cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VinaMetal, please cite it and the AutoDock Vina / AutoDock 4 foundations listed in the references."
title: VinaMetal
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/cristhianyaranganana-arch/VinaMetal"
keywords:
  - molecular docking
  - metalloprotein
  - metal coordination
  - AutoDock Vina
  - C++
authors:
  - name: "Christian Yaranga Nana"
    email: cristhianyaranganana@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5539-0526"
    affiliation: "Universidad Norbert Wiener"
abstract: >-
  VinaMetal is a fork of AutoDock Vina 1.2.7 that integrates AutoDock 4 metal
  coordination physics into the native scoring function: metal-specific 12-6
  van der Waals terms, a differentiable coordination-number penalty and a
  bounded geometry bonus, all with analytic gradients. It also detects the
  coordination sites already occupied by the rigid receptor and adjusts the
  ligand coordination-number target automatically. Redocking of GlfT2 (Mn2+)
  and PDB 1s63 (Zn2+) reproduced the crystal binding modes with heavy-atom
  RMSDs of 0.95 A and 0.33 A, respectively.
